  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\nA cold front will arrive this morning as a low moves over the \nregion. This will usher in another drop in temperatures for early \nin the week offering a relief from the heat and fire weather \nconcerns. There may be an isolated to scattered light shower or \ndry thunderstorm this through the early evening. \n\nLonger term, ensembles exit the trough to the east by Wednesday\nallowing a new ridge to establish over the Pacific Northwest. \nThis will slowly extend increasing height rises over eastern \nMontana with northwest flow aloft with a slow increase in temps.\nHIghs by Friday will reach up to 90s again and probably last into\nthe weeknight. Current ridge crest looks like it may pass the\nregion around Sunday which could introduce increased chances for\nrain thereafter. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nDeviations from NBM included using a CAMs blend for PoPs through \ntomorrow. current PPI01 is not matching up to radar echos across \nthe region and CAMs tend to continue this trend all the way into \nthis coming evening. FV3 was the one model thrown out as it was \nnot on target with current conditions. \n\nOther deviations include pulling HRRRSmoke data in for Vis to \nreplace the NBM/GLAMP data which was off target for the removal of\nthe smoke plume behind the cold front later this morning. \n\nGAH",
